Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:36:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 35/49] avformat/dashdec: keep the live position across
 manifest reloads (SegmentTimeline)

In this tree cur_seq_no is an absolute segment number (first_seq_no + index).
refresh_manifest() passed it to get_segment_start_time_based_on_timeline(),
which expects an index into the timeline, and added the *old* first_seq_no
to an index found in the *new* timeline. As a result, near the live edge:

- the previous segment was fetched again (audio/video packets repeated,
  non-monotonic timestamps),
- when the window had moved, the position jumped back by that many segments,
- when nothing matched, the position became min-1 and the "old fragment"
  path re-synced the stream.

Players show this as the picture jumping back a few seconds and audio
dropouts (seen with RTL and the yospace FAST channels, 2.5 s segments).

- $Number$ templates: the absolute number stays valid, keep it; leaving
  the window is still handled in get_current_fragment()
- other templates: map old index -> media time -> new index and add the
  new first_seq_no; a segment that is not published yet maps to the next one

Measured (4 min each, reading at the live edge, ~1900 edge waits):
repeated/rejected packets 2144-8350 -> 0, "old fragment" re-syncs 12+ -> 0
(Bauer sucht Frau / RTLup / Sky Atlantic).

Ported to FFmpeg 9.0.2 from 0003-avformat-dashdec-keep-the-live-position-across-manif.patch.
Port: rewritten by hand for the 9.0.2 helper semantics: there
get_segment_start_time_based_on_timeline() takes an absolute segment
number and calc_next_seg_no_from_timelines() returns one (upstream fix),
so refreshed_seq_no() passes/returns absolute numbers instead of adding
first_seq_no itself (same result as the 6.1 version). The upstream
fragment_timescale > 0 guard of the reload loops is kept.
---
 libavformat/dashdec.c | 64 +++++++++++++++++--------------------------
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/dashdec.c b/libavformat/dashdec.c
index 217d0eef..7c5046f7 100644
--- a/libavformat/dashdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/dashdec.c
@@ -1877,6 +1877,28 @@ static void move_segments(struct representation *rep_src, struct representation
 }
 
 
+/* Position of a representation after a manifest reload (SegmentTimeline).
+ * cur_seq_no is an absolute segment number (first_seq_no + index).
+ * $Number$ templates: the number stays valid, keep it; falling out of the
+ * window is handled later in get_current_fragment().
+ * Other templates: map via media time, old segment -> time -> new segment.
+ * In 9.0.2 get_segment_start_time_based_on_timeline() takes and
+ * calc_next_seg_no_from_timelines() returns absolute segment numbers. */
+static int64_t refreshed_seq_no(DASHContext *c, struct representation *old, struct representation *neu)
+{
+    int64_t seq_no, t;
+
+    if (old->url_template && av_stristr(old->url_template, "$Number"))
+        return old->cur_seq_no;
+
+    seq_no = FFMAX(old->cur_seq_no, old->first_seq_no);
+    t = get_segment_start_time_based_on_timeline(old, seq_no);
+    seq_no = calc_next_seg_no_from_timelines(neu, t - 1);
+    if (seq_no < 0) /* not published yet: the next segment after the new timeline */
+        seq_no = calc_max_seg_no(neu, c) + 1;
+    return seq_no;
+}
+
